# BGA Full-Stack Handoff

## Status

Completed for the requested behavior change.

## Latest Understanding

The current BGA generator is not merely reporting the wrong layer count. Its internal model assumes:

- component-local free mesh starts as `[0, 1]`
- all ignored obstacles below the mounting layer are handled as `z > 0`
- merged ignored obstacles are labeled as only `top` or `bottom`

That means the current implementation cannot represent full-stack BGA escape capacity on boards with more than two layers.

## Delivered

- Removed the static two-layer constant from `BgaTopologyGeneratorSolver`.
- Passed real `inputSrj.layerCount` through BGA initial-pattern and ignored-obstacle merge stages.
- Preserved exact obstacle `availableZ` sets during merge/trim/replacement.
- Preserved BGA layer subsets during component-node remapping back into board topology.
- Prevented lower-layer expansion nodes from overlapping multilayer replacement obstacles.
- Replaced the old two-layer BGA test contract with full-stack assertions and added remap coverage.

## Verification

- `bun test tests/component-detection-bga-only.test.ts`
- `bun test tests/repro/srj18-sample013-component-topology-connectivity.test.ts`

## Follow-On Watchpoints

- Any solver outside this path that treats `availableZ[0]` as the layer of a multilayer region should be treated as suspect in future regressions.
- The immediate benchmark focus is now the SRJ18 BGA-only subset:
  `2,6,7,8,9,10,13,14` with `--sample-timeout 600s`.
